            <ArticleTitle>Allergy to sea fishing baits.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>216-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a new case of rhinitis and asthma caused by sea fishing baits. The results showed exposure to Sipunculus nudus (Phylum Sipuncula; order Sipunculida: Sipunculidae) to be the main cause of the allergic symptoms. The intervention of IgE was demonstrated, with the presence of cross-reactions with allergenic extracts from other worm species used as baits, belonging to different orders of Annelida.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
